<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roskilde</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roskilde is a city on Zealand, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, at the head of the Roskilde Fjord. It was a royal and episcopal centre from the late tenth century, and its cathedral, built from the twelfth century, has been the burial place of Danish monarchs since the fifteenth and is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>. Five <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> ships found in the fjord are displayed in its Viking Ship Museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roskilde.jpg" alt="Roskilde" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nico/ Nils Jepsen · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RD_fra_bispegaarden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
